  "technical_audit_disposition": {
    "TA01": "Addressed in part: strain relief, open clip, post and mounted board are built, instrumented and physically validated; passive latch retention stays out of scope for this pre-release endpoint.",
    "TA02": "Addressed: a fail-closed mutation guard wraps every controller call and is demonstrated by a positive control.",
    "TA03": "Partly addressed: compiled cable mass now equals the declared target exactly and is conserved by construction; the 46-segment spatial control fails and discretisation insensitivity is NOT established.",
    "TA04": "Addressed: policy, servo and physics clocks are separated and the 4/8 kHz pair leaves job duration, servo tick count, dwell and outcome unchanged.",
    "TA05": "Addressed in part: clip, post, shelf, connector and robot contacts are separated with signed resultants reported alongside sums, and the strain-relief reaction is read from the constraint force and cross-checked against a sensor with a measured static offset. Cable tension itself is still not a named measured channel.",
    "TA06": "Addressed: native-rate abort rows plus servo-rate witness rows and full states at decision boundaries reproduce every verdict independently.",
    "TA07": "Partly addressed: achieved retreat travel, repair waypoints and per-component clipping are recorded; a commanded-norm limit is still not enforced.",
    "TA08": "Unchanged idealisation, now explicit: all arms share exact target knowledge and exact-model bias feedforward. The G2 blind first attempt is a separately labelled retrofit, not a removal of truth from the comparison arms.",
    "TA09": "Addressed: the port is mounted on standoffs over a plate, riser, shelf and support column in one common frame.",
    "TA10": "Addressed: measured throughput on the corrected task replaces the v1 extrapolation."
  },
  "cost_and_capacity": {
    "per_worker_native_steps_per_second": 3059.7,
    "twelve_worker_aggregate_native_steps_per_second": 25244.7,
    "v1_serial_baseline_native_steps_per_second": 1779.0,
    "workstation": "24 physical cores, 31.4 GB RAM, CPU MuJoCo 3.3.7",
    "note": "Measured on the corrected task with two rendered frames per request included. The per-worker rate is about 1.2x the v1 serial baseline and the twelve-worker aggregate about 14x it. No optimizer, batched environment or GPU work is included."
  },
  "scope_and_limitations": [
    "Simulation only. No hardware access, connector transfer, released retention, latching or force-certified safety claim.",
    "Fixed preset grasp and a world-fixed rigid fixture are disclosed construction boundaries; grip strength, drop recovery and fixture compliance are not measured.",
    "All arms receive full simulated state and exact-model bias feedforward. This is not camera perception.",
    "Contact channels are sums of contact force norms: positive witnesses, not net forces. Signed resultants are reported separately.",
    "Peak plug-port contact differs by about 70% between the two physics resolutions even though outcome, timing and dwell are identical, so peak contact sums must not be quoted as resolution-independent.",
    "Two physics resolutions establish insensitivity over that pair, not convergence. The spatial control failed and is preserved.",
    "The G3 screen is a small deterministic development grid with no repeated seeds, so it supports no reliability or generalisation claim.",
    "No learned model, predictor, recurrent baseline or policy was trained in this block."
  ],
  "decision": {
    "verdict": "task_and_measurement_gates_pass_learning_not_yet_earned",
    "reasoning": "The physical task, its instrumentation and its independent replay are established, and both a clip-preserving repair and a clip-releasing repair are demonstrated on real physics. But the registered G3 support is solved outright by the competent first attempt, so there is no measured residual failure and no cost deficit to justify learning on this support.",
    "next_action": "Broaden the registered support to conditions the competent first attempt cannot prevent - unmodelled mounting compliance, service loop near the measured 84.4 mm envelope, and distal catch routes that survive settling - and re-screen before any acquisition or training."
  }
